# Preview the prototype

1. Start the preview with `npm run design-space:dev` from the design space folder, unless it is
   already running.
2. Tell the designer to open http://127.0.0.1:4100/ and pick their prototype from the home page.
3. Explain what to look at: each screen, and each state of it (loading, empty, error, success)
   through the state switcher in the toolbar, and each role if the prototype has more than one.
4. If the page does not load, or a mock fails to start, say so in plain words, fix it if it is
   inside the prototype, and otherwise ask an engineer.
5. Ask what they would change. To leave notes directly on the page, they can use the feedback
   toolbar on the preview.

Next step: run `design-space-change` to apply changes and notes. When they are happy, run
`design-space-ready`.
